    "name": "Courtyard Embrace",
    "description": "A lush, lived-in garden welcome that draws guests close with leafy enclosure, softened age, and easy warmth."
  },
  "premise": {
    "title": "Courtyard Embrace",
    "register": {
      "pace": "lingering",
      "presence": "poised",
      "surfaceRichness": "layered"
    },
    "grounding": [
      "A courtyard garden interpreted with elegant ease",
      "Intimate and celebratory rather than themed or ceremonious",
      "Climbing Mediterranean greenery, garden arches, and trellises",
      "Aged tile rhythm and climbing foliage preserve an easy domestic welcome"
    ],
    "experience": "Arriving should feel immediately welcomed and surrounded by cultivated life—intimate without becoming hushed or formal.",
    "foregrounds": "The immersive courtyard garden as an intimate, easy welcome.",
    "distinctFrom": "It offers the most enveloping and hospitable choice, prioritizing the feeling of being held within the garden over citrus-led vivacity or timeworn geometric order.",
    "organizingIdea": "The garden becomes a hospitable enclosure, drawing guests inward through cultivated growth, architectural forms, and tactile age. The celebration feels already gathered around them rather than presented as a destination theme.",
    "designConsequences": [
      "Greenery and architectural garden forms create a gentle sense of enclosure.",
      "Tactile, time-softened surfaces make refinement feel lived in.",
      "Botanical detail feels immersive rather than scenic or illustrative.",
      "Formal cues remain relaxed and domestic rather than ceremonial."
    ]
  },
